 - Added `filters::enable_filter_persistent()` so Studio PostFX no longer participates in the legacy single-current-filter ownership path. Temporary stock effects can enable/disable without clearing the Studio filter.
 - Kept the original `filters::enable_filter()` behavior unchanged for compatibility with existing LG-RZ-style scripts.
 - Generated `POSTFX_INTEGRATION.txt` now uses the persistent path automatically. Existing maps that pasted an older integration snippet should regenerate/re-merge that snippet.
+
+## Pencil Sketch control cleanup + Sky Whiteness
+
+- Removed the redundant Pencil Sketch `Saturation`, `Black & White`, `Tint Strength`, and `Tint Color` controls.
+- Renamed `Color Amount` to the simpler `Color`; `0` is graphite/monochrome and `1` is the approved colored-pencil pigment.
+- Preserved the approved current default color internally with a fixed 1.08 pigment saturation, so removing the old saturation slider does not change the default look.
+- Added `Sky Whiteness` (0..1, default 0). It uses BO3 Float-Z to isolate only the extreme-far world background and pushes that region toward white paper without brightening the viewmodel or ordinary map geometry.
+- Kept `Contrast`, `Brightness`, `Depth Contour`, `Edge White`, and `Vignette` as independent finishing controls.
+- Updated the PostFX regression contract to verify the simplified Pencil controls and the new Float-Z sky mask.
+- The uploaded CI log came from commit `3ff4f01` and failed on the stale `camera movement removed` text assertion; that assertion is already absent in the current baseline (the follow-up `8f1740f` fix is included here).
